  "id": "COMPOUND:293 - PROTEIN:974",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between ertapenem and Alpha-1-acid glycoprotein 1 through a series of target interactions. ertapenem is linked to Voltage-dependent L-type calcium channel subunit beta-1, which in turn is targeted by ceftibuten and cefpiramide. Both ceftibuten and cefpiramide are also linked to Alpha-1-acid glycoprotein 1, indicating a possible downstream pathway. Similarly, ertapenem is associated with Potassium channel subfamily K member 1, which is targeted by latamoxef, which also targets Alpha-1-acid glycoprotein 1. These findings suggest that ertapenem may influence the activity of these channels, which in turn modulate the expression or function of Alpha-1-acid glycoprotein 1. The evidence supports a mechanism where ertapenem could indirectly affect Alpha-1-acid glycoprotein 1 through its interaction with these channels, though the exact nature of this relationship remains to be fully elucidated.",
